# Where the app should reach the FastAPI backend.
# Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable at build time.
#
# Development (Expo Go): your computer LAN IP - find it with `ipconfig` / `ifconfig`
# Production (APK):      your public tunnel URL
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and set the value. Without it the app falls back to
# the defaults baked into src/api/client.ts.
#
# NOTE: Metro replaces process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL with a literal and then
# strips the unused fallback branches. So whatever is in .env at bundle time is
# what the build talks to - a LAN IP baked into an APK will not work for anyone
# outside your Wi-Fi. `.env` is gitignored, so EAS Build does not upload it and
# a cloud build correctly falls back to the tunnel URL.
#
# Env vars are inlined at BUNDLE time: restart `npx expo start` after changing
# this, a reload is not enough.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8000

# --- Escape hatch (SDK 56+) ---
# Since SDK 56, Expo installs its own WinterCG `expo/fetch` as globalThis.fetch.
# Every request in client.ts sends a plain string body, which both implementations
# handle identically, so this should not be needed. If you ever hit a networking
# oddity that disappears on SDK 55, uncomment this to restore React Native's fetch.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_RN_FETCH=1
